# The reviewed checks by role NAME (ADR-0059 decision 7, "Checks by role
# name", story R0.13). Read by internal/api/role_name_literals_test.go, which
# fails on a site of `super_admin` or `admin` that is not listed here and on
# a row whose site is gone. The web client has its own list,
# apps/elitea-web/src/pages/admin/roleNameLiterals.reviewed.json.
#
# What is scanned: every non-test Go file of services/elitea-main and every
# .sql query file, outside any directory named migrations (migrations/ and the
# bootstrap schema internal/infra/db/migrations: applied migrations are
# immutable, so what they seed is data the rows below act on) and testdata/.
# Generated code (sqlcgen) is scanned too and carries the decision of its
# .sql source.
#
# Row: file | scope | form | count | decision | why
#   form: literal:<name> (a Go string equal to the name), sql:<name> (a SQL
#         literal inside a Go string or a .sql query), const:<Name> (a
#         comparison with a constant whose value is the name).
#   decision:
#     kept      the check tests the name on purpose (the ADR's "Kept").
#     compat    kept for one release beside the role set (R0.8b), removed with
#               the field it serves (R0.8c, issue 2586).
#     seed      the name is data (a built-in role, a default); no check here
#               decides access by it.
#     project   a PROJECT role name (auth_core__project_role), the owner role
#               of a project; ADR-0059 does not change the project roles.
#     unrelated the string is not a role name.
#
# Replaced by R0.13 (no longer in the source): the priority ordering of the
# Users listing (users.go adminRolePriority in the listing SQL) is gone, the
# listing returns the set by name; currentAdminRole was removed by R0.8b and
# the demotion guard tests admin.auth.users.super_admin
# (adminaccess.Caller.SuperAdmin), not the caller's role name. R0.8c removed
# the listing's single `admin_role` field and its legacyAdminRoleOrder.

# ── The ADR's table ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
internal/infra/db/projectaccess/projectaccess.go | func Membership | sql:super_admin | 1 | kept | The standing administration role named super_admin passes the project access check of every project. An elevation gives permissions, not the name, and a custom role is not the name: neither passes (middleware/project_authorization_elevation_postgres_integration_test.go). Break-glass repairs the platform; it does not open project content.
internal/api/v2/eliteacore/handler.go | const usersCountQuery | sql:super_admin | 1 | kept | Holders of the standing super_admin are counted as members of every project; same scope as projectaccess.Membership.
internal/api/v2/eliteacore/handler.go | const usersPageQuery | sql:super_admin | 2 | kept | Holders of the standing super_admin are listed as members of every project (roles ARRAY['super_admin']); same scope as projectaccess.Membership.
internal/db/queries/auth_provisioning.sql | query HasAuthAdministrationAdminRole | sql:admin | 1 | kept | admin or super_admin gets the extra project roles at public-project enrollment; narrow roles do not.
internal/db/queries/auth_provisioning.sql | query HasAuthAdministrationAdminRole | sql:super_admin | 1 | kept | As above: the two names, by decision.
internal/db/sqlcgen/auth_provisioning.sql.go | const hasAuthAdministrationAdminRole | sql:admin | 1 | kept | Generated from auth_provisioning.sql HasAuthAdministrationAdminRole.
internal/db/sqlcgen/auth_provisioning.sql.go | const hasAuthAdministrationAdminRole | sql:super_admin | 1 | kept | Generated from auth_provisioning.sql HasAuthAdministrationAdminRole.

# ── The super_admin role as the TARGET of a write ───────────────────────────
# Giving or taking the role named super_admin needs the permission
# admin.auth.users.super_admin; the caller is tested by the permission, the
# role being given or taken is named.
internal/api/v2/admin/users.go | func (Handler).setAdminRole | const:adminaccess.SuperAdminRole | 2 | kept | The early guard: the difference gives or takes super_admin, so the caller must hold admin.auth.users.super_admin (resolveAssigningCaller).
internal/api/v2/admin/users.go | func (Handler).checkCentralRoles | const:adminaccess.SuperAdminRole | 1 | kept | The same guard under the role-writes lock; tests caller.SuperAdmin, the permission.
internal/api/v2/admin/modes.go | func (Handler).ModesAssign | const:adminaccess.SuperAdminRole | 1 | kept | Assigning super_admin on the modes route needs the permission.
internal/adminaccess/role_definition.go | func (Assigner).guards | const:SuperAdminRole | 1 | kept | The role definitions read (R3.9a) answers what checkCentralRoles would: giving or taking super_admin needs admin.auth.users.super_admin; tests caller.SuperAdmin, the permission.
internal/api/v2/admin/modes.go | func (Handler).ModesRemove | literal:super_admin | 1 | kept | Removing super_admin on the modes route needs the permission, in every mode a legacy database carries the name in.
internal/adminaccess/policy.go | const SuperAdminRole | literal:super_admin | 1 | kept | The role that alone may hold admin.auth.users.super_admin (ADR-0059 decision 3); the constant the guards above name.
internal/adminaccess/policy.go | func CheckReserved | const:SuperAdminRole | 1 | kept | admin.auth.users.super_admin is reserved to the role named super_admin: the matrix adds it to no other role (migrations/super_admin_permission_holders_postgres_integration_test.go).

# ── Names as data ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
internal/adminaccess/builtin_roles.go | const RoleSuperAdmin | literal:super_admin | 1 | seed | The built-in role catalogue (R0.7): the name of a seeded role and its set.
internal/adminaccess/builtin_roles.go | const RoleAdmin | literal:admin | 1 | seed | The built-in role catalogue (R0.7).
internal/api/v2/admin/roles_crud.go | var codeNamedRoles | literal:super_admin | 1 | seed | Refuses to rename or delete a role this list names, because the kept sites above name it; it grants nothing.
internal/api/v2/admin/roles_crud.go | var codeNamedRoles | literal:admin | 1 | seed | As above.
internal/application/identity/provision.go | const InitialAdministrationRole | literal:super_admin | 1 | seed | The role the bootstrap-only initial administrators receive (R0.12b); it is assigned, not tested.

